+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, but Filtering the Directory Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was a deliberate decision stayed open.
+
+A request on 2026-11-04 asks to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty. Read against the original row, that request falls inside a declined capability. The owner decided the row at intake, in these words: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter. Rejected by the owner's decision above.
+2. **Remove NG-9.** Open every kind of search over pets, visits, and veterinarians. Not requested; the decision keeps free-text veterinarian search out.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined, and so do pet and visit search. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed, not withdrawn. The veterinarian directory may be filtered by an attribute it already shows. Specialty is the first and only such filter requested, specified as REQ-VET-003. Free-text veterinarian search remains a non-goal. Pet and visit search are unchanged by this decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- REQ-VET-003 can proceed without contradicting the Non-Goals table.
+- A later filter on another shown attribute needs its own requirement, but not a further change to NG-9.
+- The line between a filter and a free-text search is drawn by this ADR's quote; a request that blurs it returns to the owner.
+- NG-9 is now a decided row and leaves the open provenance consultation recorded in the Non-Goals preamble.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
