+# Specialty Filter as an Uncached Repository Query
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+REQ-VET-003 narrows both veterinarian list surfaces to the veterinarians holding one named specialty. Matching is on the whole name and ignores letter case. The narrowed HTML page is paged; the machine-readable list is not.
+
+Two facts about the existing code shape the choice. The veterinarian repository's read methods are cached in one cache with no size limit and no eviction. Case-insensitive matching on last name already diverges by vendor, because it relies on column type and collation rather than the query.
+
+The specialty value is caller-chosen text. Anything keyed on it grows with the number of distinct values a caller sends.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Filter in memory over the cached full list.** A predicate on `Vet` selects the matches; the controller pages the result itself. Keeps the cache, but hand-writes paging and diverges from the owner search pattern.
+2. **Cached repository query.** A derived query on `VetRepository`, cached like the existing reads. Each distinct caller value adds a cache entry to an unbounded cache, a memory-exhaustion vector.
+3. **Uncached repository query** (chosen). A derived query on `VetRepository` with case-insensitive comparison in the query itself, and no cache annotation.
+
+## Decision
+
+The narrowing is a Spring Data derived query on `VetRepository`, one paged and one unpaged variant. The comparison ignores case in the generated SQL, so it holds on H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL alike. The narrowed queries carry no cache annotation. A caller-supplied value never becomes a key in the veterinarian cache.
+
+This follows the owner search, which is also a paged derived query on its repository. A later filter on another shown attribute, which NG-9 as narrowed admits, follows the same form.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Matching semantics live in one declarative query, testable against the real database.
+- Case-insensitivity does not depend on vendor collation, unlike the owner search defect.
+- Every narrowed request reaches the database. At the clinic's size this is a small join, recorded in the design's Scale and Load table.
+- The unfiltered reads stay cached, so requests without a specialty behave as before.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [System design: Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts)
+- [System design: Scale and Load](../system-design.md#scale-and-load)
+- [Non-goal ADR narrowing NG-9](2026-11-04-non-goal-veterinarian-search-narrowed.md)
